  source/blender/blenkernel/intern/brush.cc
      -> factors.js      the ten distance falloff presets
      -> cache.js        which brushes offer Accumulate
  source/blender/editors/sculpt_paint/mesh/mesh_paint.cc
      -> symmetry.js     the mirror passes, valid pass combinations, symmetry feather
  source/blender/editors/sculpt_paint/paint_intern.hh
      -> symmetry.js     symmetry_flip, is_symmetry_iteration_valid
  source/blender/editors/sculpt_paint/mesh/brushes/smooth.cc
  source/blender/editors/sculpt_paint/mesh/brushes/enhance_details.cc
  source/blender/editors/sculpt_paint/mesh/sculpt_smooth.cc
      -> smooth.js, brushes/smooth.js   pass splitting, the border and corner rule, Enhance Details
  source/blender/editors/sculpt_paint/mesh/brushes/draw.cc      -> brushes/draw.js (Draw, Nudge)
  source/blender/editors/sculpt_paint/mesh/brushes/inflate.cc   -> brushes/inflate.js
  source/blender/editors/sculpt_paint/mesh/brushes/grab.cc      -> brushes/grab.js
  source/blender/editors/sculpt_paint/mesh/sculpt_undo.cc       -> undo.js (the first-touch model)

Brush kernels added later (brushes/set-a.js, brushes/set-b.js) name their own sources in their
file headers; the list above is what exists today.

presets.json is a measurement of Blender 5.2.1's Essentials brush library
(datafiles/assets/brushes/essentials_brushes-mesh_sculpt.blend), dumped headless.
scripts/blender-ref.py records golden strokes from the same build for the parity tests.

